  "title": "Native far sides through plane glue",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Native far sides through plane glue (computed on the 191 saved and 86 fresh maps, reading only K4^(3), the Fano plane and census 58, which ticket A shows do not depend on gluing). Every Fano atom acts as one on these far sides (1,065 of 1,065). All 372 pairs of lines of different atoms that are twins of the yes/no creation relation (39 spaces) are told apart by them; for 114 of these pairs the only difference lies in their rows at lines outside the atoms, where lines of one atom can differ too. Twins on the gluing-free rows at atom lines read the atoms of 234 of the 277 spaces (the yes/no two-stage rule: 219), merging atoms in 38 and splitting or dropping one in 5; twins on rows and columns read only 11, because an atom's lines differ in what they receive.",
